            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I found no concrete production failure caused by this candidate.",
              "Rewrite appends the block only when it is non-empty and the prompt doesn't already contain it, so a retried or repeated hook call changes nothing. An empty prompt is still left alone.",
              "DecodeAgentCall reads cwd leniently. A missing, null or wrongly typed cwd becomes an empty string and never causes a decode error, so Agent calls the baseline could rewrite still work.",
              "OnInstructions is read-only. It never removes a closed workflow's binding. A binding-store failure returns a warning or silence instead of a panic.",
              "InstructionsBlock returns one line when the plan can't be computed, and it sanitizes and bounds its output.",
              "The extra work per Agent call is one binding load and one workflow load, which is small and not a measurable load or latency problem.",
              "The ADR describes the settings and cmd wiring, and the 'memory plan --instructions' command. Those paths are not in this candidate, so I could not review them."
            ]
