            "evidence": [
              "The gate rewrite is unchanged when Config.Instructions is empty. engine/gate/instructions_test.go checks this for contract types, unknown types and an empty type.",
              "Appending the block twice is prevented by the strings.Contains check in appendInstructions. engine/gate/instructions_test.go asserts idempotence for prompts with and without trailing newlines.",
              "DecodeAgentCall reads cwd as raw JSON and drops it when it is not a string. A missing, null, numeric or object cwd therefore does not cause an error, so calls that decoded before still decode. engine/hookwire/sessionstart_test.go covers these cases.",
              "OnInstructions is read-only. It never unbinds, and it does not query the workflow store when nothing is bound. engine/projection/app/instructions_test.go covers both.",
              "The OnPrompt refactor into readBound keeps the same order of outcomes: silence, then the store warning, then the workflow load. The existing OnPrompt tests are not in this patch, so I did not see them re-run.",
              "InstructionsBlock sanitizes every value it writes, and its tests cover a goal containing a newline. An uncomputable plan gives one line, and scope none and scope project are tested.",
              "This is a partial implementation: the ledger marks M6b and M6c as not done, so the missing wiring is not a defect of this patch. The patch contains no code for installing the hook, for `memory plan --instructions`, or for the gate-task caller."
